# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Docker sends the whole context to the daemon before it reads a single
# instruction, so anything listed here is a cost paid on every build of every
# image whether or not a Dockerfile would have used it. Without this file the
# context was 20GB — build artefacts and git worktrees, none of which any image
# copies — and sending it took longer than compiling.
#
# Each entry is something that is either rebuilt inside the image or has no
# business in one.

# Rust build artefacts. The images compile from source; a host target directory
# is both useless to them and the single largest thing in the tree.
api/target/

# BuildKit reads the Runtime Dockerfile as the recipe. Keep package pins out
# of the Cargo planner and compiler COPY inputs.
api/crates/layer4-runtime/Dockerfile

# Installed and generated by the web image itself.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/

# Agent worktrees and tool state. Each worktree is a full checkout with its own
# build artefacts, so a handful of them outweighs the repository many times over.
.claude/
.gstack/

# History, not source. Nothing in any image reads it.
.git
**/.git
.github/*
!.github/scripts/
.github/scripts/*
!.github/scripts/bubblewrap-loopback.patch
!.github/scripts/bubblewrap-loopback-test.c
!.github/scripts/bubblewrap-openat2.patch
!.github/scripts/bubblewrap-openat2-test.c

# Editor and platform leavings.
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Public images must never receive workstation or CI credentials, including
# files in nested dependency directories. Build authentication uses BuildKit
# secret mounts; runtime credentials come from chrono-cd secret declarations.
.env*
**/.env*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.netrc
**/.netrc
.git-credentials
**/.git-credentials
.docker
**/.docker
.ssh
**/.ssh
.gnupg
**/.gnupg
.pypirc
**/.pypirc
.kube
**/.kube
kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
**/kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig
**/*.kubeconfig
.aws
**/.aws
.azure
**/.azure
.config/gcloud
**/.config/gcloud
.config/gh
**/.config/gh
credentials
**/credentials
credentials.json
**/credentials.json
application_default_credentials.json
**/application_default_credentials.json

# Private deployment inputs and internal documentation stay outside GitHub.
/infra/
/docs/
/sdk/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
